266
00:12:33,830 --> 00:12:37,080
we're both hardcore into quilting.

267
00:12:39,470 --> 00:12:41,470
Your words fall like acid rain

268
00:12:41,470 --> 00:12:44,110
on the wounded petals of my heart.

269
00:12:46,490 --> 00:12:47,380
That's Sheldon.

270
00:12:47,380 --> 00:12:49,820
He says he'll be down in a minute.

271
00:12:50,540 --> 00:12:51,710
What are you doing?

272
00:12:51,930 --> 00:12:54,110
Oh, he's not coming out until he sees proof

273
00:12:54,110 --> 00:12:56,980
you don't have an air freshener in your car.

274
00:12:58,410 --> 00:13:00,870
This is gonna be a long weekend for you.

275
00:13:00,870 --> 00:13:02,760
You're the reason I'm doing it!

276
00:13:02,760 --> 00:13:04,680
I said to stop insulting each other.

277
00:13:04,680 --> 00:13:07,890
I didn't tell you to take him on a romantic getaway.

278
00:13:09,180 --> 00:13:10,850
How do I know what you said?

279
00:13:10,850 --> 00:13:14,250
Damn you and your noise-cancelling breasts.

280
00:13:16,760 --> 00:13:17,800
Hello.

281
00:13:17,800 --> 00:13:19,620
- Hi. - Hey, buddy.

282
00:13:20,290 --> 00:13:21,700
You excited for Texas?

283
00:13:21,700 --> 00:13:23,490
Oh, very much so.

284
00:13:23,490 --> 00:13:27,060
It's not every day you get to tour NASA with a real astronaut.

285
00:13:27,060 --> 00:13:30,160
Who's the real astronaut?

286
00:13:32,650 --> 00:13:34,000
Buzz Aldrin.

287
00:13:34,000 --> 00:13:36,340
Oh. Yay!

288
00:13:49,190 --> 00:13:50,310
Howard?

289
00:13:50,840 --> 00:13:51,590
Howard?

290
00:13:52,180 --> 00:13:53,590
Howard?

291
00:13:56,120 --> 00:13:57,960
What now?

292
00:13:58,990 --> 00:14:00,130
I have to go to the bathroom.

293
00:14:00,130 --> 00:14:01,180
You just went to the bathroom.

294
00:14:01,180 --> 00:14:04,530
I didn't use it because it didn't seem safe.

295
00:14:04,940 --> 00:14:08,860
Despite all my e-mails, the toilet didn't have a seatbelt.

296
00:14:10,170 --> 00:14:11,790
Well, it still doesn't.

297
00:14:11,790 --> 00:14:14,640
I realize that, but safety concerns went out the window

298
00:14:14,640 --> 00:14:16,620
two apple juices ago.

299
00:14:17,840 --> 00:14:19,560
Fine.

300
00:14:21,010 --> 00:14:22,170
Why are you getting annoyed?

301
00:14:22,170 --> 00:14:24,840
I'm trying to be a better friend,

302
00:14:24,840 --> 00:14:29,070
but you constantly say and do irritating things.

303
00:14:29,070 --> 00:14:30,940
- Like when? - When?!

304
00:14:30,940 --> 00:14:31,890
How about in the car?

305
00:14:31,890 --> 00:14:34,350
I'm an astronaut, and you know it.

306
00:14:34,350 --> 00:14:37,740
You just don't like admitting it, because you're jealous.

307
00:14:39,760 --> 00:14:42,770
Well, truth be told,

308
00:14:42,770 --> 00:14:45,490
as a child, I did dream of going to space.

309
00:14:45,490 --> 00:14:47,610
Those astronauts were my heroes.

310
00:14:47,610 --> 00:14:49,040
And...

311
00:14:49,040 --> 00:14:52,640
when you got to go, it was hard for me.

312
00:14:54,900 --> 00:14:56,060
Thank you.

313
00:14:56,060 --> 00:14:57,080
Because it made me realize

314
00:14:57,080 --> 00:14:59,320
they'll just send anyone up there.

315
00:15:01,780 --> 00:15:03,560
- Aren't you going to let me out? - No.

316
00:15:03,560 --> 00:15:05,640
But I still need to use the bathroom.

317
00:15:05,640 --> 00:15:07,860
Here you go. Be creative.

318
00:15:11,300 --> 00:15:13,940
What's the matter? Scared of a little turbulence?

319
00:15:13,940 --> 00:15:17,340
No, turbulence is just the equalization

320
00:15:17,340 --> 00:15:20,180
of diurnal temperature variations in the atmosphere.

321
00:15:20,180 --> 00:15:22,080
I'm not scared at all.

322
00:15:22,720 --> 00:15:25,200
Oh, apple juice, stay where you are.

323
00:15:26,530 --> 00:15:27,870
Oh, this is nothing.

324
00:15:27,870 --> 00:15:29,230
I experienced way worse

325
00:15:29,230 --> 00:15:31,090
when I was plummeting back to Earth,

326
00:15:31,090 --> 00:15:34,460
apparently not being a real astronaut.

327
00:15:35,970 --> 00:15:38,180
Okay, that was a big one.

328
00:15:39,720 --> 00:15:41,300
I take it back. I'm scared of turbulence!

329
00:15:41,300 --> 00:15:43,120
I'm gonna need that bag back.

330
00:15:47,000 --> 00:15:48,360
You sure you want to do this?

331
00:15:48,360 --> 00:15:50,540
Yeah. Why wouldn't I want to get my old job back?

332
00:15:50,540 --> 00:15:52,120
It'll be fun to see everyone.

333
00:15:52,120 --> 00:15:53,670
I haven't talked to them since I said,

334
00:15:53,670 --> 00:15:56,960
"I quit. See you at the Oscars, bitches."

335
00:15:57,780 --> 00:15:59,660
Come on, let's just get this over with.

336
00:15:59,660 --> 00:16:01,120
"Let's get this over with."

337
00:16:01,120 --> 00:16:02,780
Am I driving you to the Cheesecake Factory,

338
00:16:02,780 --> 00:16:04,710
or are we having sex?

339
00:16:06,070 --> 00:16:07,770
I'm just... I'm trying to lighten the mood.

340
00:16:07,770 --> 00:16:09,620
- I know. Thank you. - Sorry.

341
00:16:09,620 --> 00:16:11,160
It's just so humiliating.

342
00:16:11,160 --> 00:16:12,730
So humiliating?

343
00:16:12,730 --> 00:16:14,310
Am I driving you to the Cheesecake Factory...?

344
00:16:14,310 --> 00:16:16,720
I'm sorry. I'll-I'll stop. I'll stop.

345
00:16:19,070 --> 00:16:21,000
Come on, don't look so sad.

346
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:22,080
You never know what's gonna happen.

347
00:16:22,080 --> 00:16:23,420
Maybe tonight will be great.

348
00:16:23,420 --> 00:16:25,140
Sweetie, I know you're trying to make me feel better,

349
00:16:25,140 --> 00:16:26,000
and I love you for that,

350
00:16:26,000 --> 00:16:28,720
but it's making me feel worse, and I kind of hate you.

351
00:16:31,760 --> 00:16:32,960
This isn't your car.

352
00:16:32,960 --> 00:16:36,440
I know. I thought we'd take yours.

353
00:16:38,500 --> 00:16:40,380
I don't understand.

354
00:16:40,990 --> 00:16:43,280
It's nothing fancy, but it'll get you to auditions,

355
00:16:43,280 --> 00:16:46,950
and at least for now, you don't have to go back to waitressing.

356
00:16:48,700 --> 00:16:51,010
I don't know what to say.

357
00:16:52,300 --> 00:16:53,920
Don't say anything.

358
00:16:53,920 --> 00:16:56,180
Oh, my God.

359
00:16:56,800 --> 00:16:57,990
I mean, you could say, "thank you."

360
00:16:57,990 --> 00:17:00,270
I did just buy you a car.

361
00:17:04,850 --> 00:17:06,580
Look, I admit that it's odd

362
00:17:06,580 --> 00:17:08,460
that Rajesh didn't write to you himself,

363
00:17:08,460 --> 00:17:09,710
but if you get to know him,

364
00:17:09,710 --> 00:17:13,010
you'll see he's just a sweet, regular guy.

365
00:17:13,010 --> 00:17:14,330
As a counterpoint, here he is,

366
00:17:14,330 --> 00:17:16,710
uninvited and visibly sweaty.

367
00:17:16,710 --> 00:17:18,420
- Hello, Emily. - Hello.

368
00:17:18,420 --> 00:17:19,770
Amy told me you were concerned that

369
00:17:19,770 --> 00:17:22,450
I might be too passive and shy.

370
00:17:22,450 --> 00:17:24,150
Let me ask you something.

371
00:17:24,150 --> 00:17:25,830
Would a passive guy barge in here

372
00:17:25,830 --> 00:17:28,380
to look you in the eye and say,

373
00:17:28,380 --> 00:17:31,670
"Hey, dew-kissed flower, what's up?"

374
00:17:35,310 --> 00:17:38,460
No, but a weird guy with no boundaries might.

375
00:17:38,460 --> 00:17:40,190
Uh, okay, that's a separate issue.

376
00:17:40,190 --> 00:17:42,970
Let's put a pin in that and just focus on the passive thing.

377
00:17:42,970 --> 00:17:44,230
I'm leaving.

378
00:17:44,230 --> 00:17:46,490
Are we still going to go to that Chaucer reading Friday?

379
00:17:46,490 --> 00:17:48,970
You know, I think I'm just gonna go by myself.

380
00:17:52,220 --> 00:17:54,740
Not my best first date.

381
00:17:56,300 --> 00:17:58,450
Yeah, but not my worst, either.

382
00:18:02,960 --> 00:18:05,150
I'm sorry for every mean thing I ever did or said to you!

383
00:18:05,150 --> 00:18:07,310
I'm sorry, too! It's all my fault!

384
00:18:08,920 --> 00:18:10,120
If you weren't my friend,

385
00:18:10,120 --> 00:18:11,780
there'd be a hole in my life!

386
00:18:11,790 --> 00:18:13,450
Thank you, Sheldon.

387
00:18:13,450 --> 00:18:16,180
Kind of like when Firefly was cancelled.

388
00:18:16,590 --> 00:18:19,130
But not as big.

389
00:18:26,220 --> 00:18:28,630
The captain has turned off the fasten seat belt sign.

390
00:18:28,630 --> 00:18:31,740
You're now free to move about the cabin.

391
00:18:32,260 --> 00:18:34,490
- It's over. - Yeah.

392
00:18:37,070 --> 00:18:41,340
Should we stop holding hands now?

393
00:18:42,630 --> 00:18:45,190
- In a minute. - Okay, good.

